<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tomyris</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tomyris was a queen of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massagetae">Massagetae</a>, a nomadic Iranian people east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>, in the 6th century BCE. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> captured her son by a trick, she defeated the Persian army in 530 BCE, killed Cyrus and had his head put in a wineskin filled with blood.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tomyris.jpg" alt="Tomyris" width="320" height="508" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrea del Castagno · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tomyris-Castagno.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
